  "id": "COMPOUND:28009 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Charantoside V may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of target relationships. This is supported by the fact that Charantoside V is directly linked to DMS-79, which in turn is a target of Albaflavenone and Pseudopterosin P. All three of these compounds are known to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a potential pathway through which Charantoside V could influence this complex. The scores assigned to these relationships are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological connection. The evidence is strengthened by the shared target of the three compounds, which implies a possible mechanism of action involving the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. However, the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct relationship between Charantoside V and the complex.",
